17. Interview Questions
=======================

Q1. What is a function template?

A generic function that works with multiple data types using one
implementation.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Why use function templates?

• Code reuse
• Less duplication
• Compile-time polymorphism
• Type safety

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Difference between function overloading and function templates?

Function Overloading
--------------------
• Multiple implementations
• Different parameter lists
• More duplicate code

Function Template
-----------------
• Single generic implementation
• Compiler generates required versions
• Less duplicate code

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Difference between typename and class?

No difference.

Both are equivalent in template parameter lists.

Modern C++ style prefers:

template<typename T>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. What is template instantiation?

The process where the compiler generates an actual function from a template
for a specific type.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. When does template instantiation happen?

At compile time.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. Can function templates be overloaded?

Yes.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. Can a normal function and a template function coexist?

Yes.

The compiler prefers the normal function if both are equally good matches.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q9. Can template arguments be deduced automatically?

Yes.

The compiler usually deduces the template parameters from function arguments.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Why are template implementations usually placed in header files?

Because the compiler must see the complete template definition during
instantiation. Otherwise, linker errors occur.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q11. Can a function template have multiple template parameters?

Yes.

Example

template<typename T, typename U>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q12. Can function templates have default template arguments?

Yes.

Example

template<typename T = int>

---------------------------------------------------------

18. Common Mistakes
==================

❌ Mixing incompatible types without using multiple template parameters.

❌ Assuming templates generate code before they are used.

❌ Forgetting that operations inside templates must be valid for all types.

❌ Defining template implementations only in .cpp files.

---------------------------------------------------------

